<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44705" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">somnĭfer</span></b> , ĕra,
			ĕrum, adj.
		somnus-fero, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>sleep-bringing</i>, <i>soporific</i>,
				<i>somniferous</i> (<b>poet.</b>
			and in post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vis papaveris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 25, 61, § 229</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virga (Mercurii),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					1, 672</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aspis,</span>”
				<i>causing torpidity</i>, <i>deadly</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					9, 701</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venenum (aspidis),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					9, 693</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">strychnos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Flor. 74</span></i>
			; cf. somniculosus, II., and somnificus.</div>
